  9    1645708  jdev-Pri-Elf-Mal-Cha died on the Astral Plane.                 
                Killed by a priest of Moloch (with the Amulet).         -  [96]

Sigh.  So I decided to try playing a priest, and the first time, I
thought I was toast when I angered Anhur by praying about how I was
fainting from hunger too soon after praying about almost dying in
combat.  But I came back, by eating garlic and wolfsbane, then hunting
down and eating a housecat (yes, I know about the penalty for that).
And then a bones file with [SB and a magic lamp, plus a little
beneficence from the RNG (e.g., decent spellbooks, and 8 wraith
corpses on the Quest (though Nalzok was a little touch-and-go, before
a strategic retreat turned the tide)), did the rest.

And then this.  So, stuff I can see I could have done better:

1) Not blowing all my crowd control during that unfortunate incident
   on Air with the ki-rin that Rodney so helpfully sent me, and all
   its summoning.

2) Not letting some of the other crowd control items get toasted by
   lightning blasts (oh, while I'm here, a question: does reflection
   prevent that?  Some perfectly good rings blew up that way, too).

3) Not getting confused (out-of-game) and wasting a bunch of marker
   charges on unnecessary ?oEA at the Castle when they could have gone
   on, say, ?oCharging for a wand of death.

4) Using jumping, maybe using two-weapon instead of a shield, reverse
   genocide (say, for nurse dancing; I lost 150+ HP during my three
   kills of Death), or other bits of subtlety I know about but didn't
   do.  Or just more altar camping, for the death drops if nothing else.

5) Applying my blindfold when the Archon situation emerged, so they
   couldn't stun me.

Probably more.  Also, I've found that "oLS are in fact useful; the two
I had helped me mow my way out of the two-Riders-and-a-summon-storm
incident on the way back from the central altar, and if I'd had more
HP, or a relevant half-damage item (which I think == the Key), or more
!oFH, or ... then I might even have made it there.

Oh well.  Nothing to do but try again.


